WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.240
Alright people, we're taking a break from
politics this week and focusing on the F word,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.240
that's right, Food.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.930
They say you are what you eat and if that's
true, a lot of us are half hot dog, half pizza

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.230
and half ice cream.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.490
I know that's three halves but we're a pretty
fat bunch of people these days.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:26.660
Every week there's a new diet to follow, a
new oil to avoid, or a new super food that'll

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:27.730
change you life.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.929
Then the week after that, we usually find
out this new revolutionary diet will actually

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:36.620
made you gain weight, you actually need that
oil to live, and the super food does absolutely

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.620
nothing.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.940
Add an endless slew of magazines to the countless
websites and blogs devoted to keeping you

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.620
clicking on the newest fad and it becomes
almost impossible to figure out what you should

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.620
eat.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.350
As those of you who follow me on social media
know, I'm in the midst of a little diet myself

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.350
right now.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:57.830
I'm doing a slow-carb paleo diet which is
a slightly modified version of what former

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.940
Rubin Report guest Tim Ferris helped popularize.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.950
Basically I'm eating only meat, fish, and
veggies, with no sugar and very limited carbs.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:11.020
I'm even putting grass fed butter in my coffee
to get an extra boost of fat and energy in

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.080
the morning.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.310
As of taping this Direct Message, I've lost
about 5 pounds in 10 days.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:20.430
I've also punched 4 random strangers on the
street for looking at me the wrong way...but

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.220
as they say, everything in moderation.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.520
Of course what you should or shouldn't put
in your body isn't just about weight.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.090
It's also about your mind.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:32.100
And this is a place where the science is actually
pretty solid.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.870
The foods we eat, or don't eat, can have a
tremendous affect on our brain itself, right

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:39.060
down to our ability to think.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.810
As we've seen a spike in degenerative brains
diseases such as Alzheimers and Parkinson's

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:48.370
Disease, which are just two of the many forms
of dementia, it's becoming clearer and clearer

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:54.270
that fueling our brains with the right foods
and avoiding the wrong ones are a key to brain

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.350
health.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.770
So much of what we talk about on this show
is related to to clear and critical thinking.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:05.320
While we may not think about how food is affecting
our brains on a daily basis, feeding our brains

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.959
the right foods as as important, actually
probably more important than feeding our brains

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:12.060
the right information.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.270
So this week we're gonna learn some information
on what we should feed our brains so that

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:22.160
we're optimized to engage in intellectual
battles in the best way possible.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:26.190
Joining me to discuss this is an old friend
of the show and author of the new book Genius

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.820
Foods, Max Lugavere.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.220
Now excuse me while I put grass fed butter
on an avocado sprinkled with goji berries

